  <section class="block wrap" id="ships">
    <div class="sec-head"><h2>How this site ships</h2><p>This page is deployed by the same kind of pipeline I build. The panel on the right reads live from the running server.</p></div>
    <div class="ships">
      <ol class="pipe">
        <li><div><h3>Push to GitHub</h3><p>A commit to <code>main</code> starts both the CI workflow and a Render deploy.</p></div></li>
        <li><div><h3>Build and smoke-test in CI</h3><p>GitHub Actions builds the Docker image, starts the container and checks <code>/</code>, <code>/healthz</code> and the CV download.</p></div></li>
        <li><div><h3>Multi-stage Docker build</h3><p>The .NET SDK image compiles the app. Only the slim ASP.NET runtime ships, running as a non-root user.</p></div></li>
        <li><div><h3>Deploy on Render</h3><p>Render builds from the same Dockerfile and waits for <code>/healthz</code> before sending traffic to the new version.</p></div></li>
        <li><div><h3>Serve, hardened</h3><p>Security headers, a content security policy, compression and cached static files on every response.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="live" aria-live="polite">
        <div class="live-head"><span>GET /api/info</span><span class="state" id="live-state">● checking…</span></div>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Health</dt><dd id="live-health">…</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Deployed commit</dt><dd id="live-commit">…</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Branch</dt><dd id="live-branch">…</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Runtime</dt><dd id="live-runtime">…</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Container up for</dt><dd id="live-uptime">…</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Response time</dt><dd id="live-latency">…</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <div class="live-foot">On Render's free plan the container sleeps when idle, so the first visit can take up to a minute.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

